  "overview": {
    "id": "overview",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 80,
    "width": 1400,
    "height": 130,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "25px"
    },
    "html": "Two things about <b>holder</b> are easy to get wrong. A <b>count</b> is spent on every widget the holder names separately, the way FLIP and ROTATE always did it &ndash; which is why the routine editor words it &quot;1 widget in each of&quot; &ndash; while naming the same widgets with <b>target</b> spends it once in total. And a <b>seat</b> contributes what lies in its hand and belongs to its player, so an empty seat contributes nothing. Put a button into edit mode and press ctrl-j to read the routine behind it."
  },
